-- title:
--   Rigidity for formal mathcal O_D-modules from p-adic density
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $L$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is nilpotent, and let $X$, $X'$ be formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules over $L$ in the sense of the project's structure `FormalODModule`: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $L$, together with pairs of power series $\mathrm{act}\,a$ ($a$ in $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$, realised as the Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{p^2}$) and $\varpi$, each an endomorphism of the law, with $\mathrm{act}\,1$ the identity, $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive for the law, $\varpi\circ\varpi=\mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\varpi\circ\mathrm{act}\,a=\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{Frob}\,a)\circ\varpi$. Let $D$ be a subset of $\mathbb Z_{p^2}\times\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ which is $p$-adically dense, in the form: for every $k$ and every $(\alpha,\beta)$ there is $d\in D$ with $d_1-\alpha$ and $d_2-\beta$ in the ideal generated by $p^k$. Let $t$ assign, to every commutative $L$-algebra $C$ and ideal $J\subseteq C$, a map from pairs to pairs of elements of $C$, subject to the following for nilpotent $J$ and arguments with all entries in $J$: $t_{C,J}(x)$ again has entries in $J$; $t$ is natural along $L$-algebra maps $\varphi\colon C\to C'$ carrying $J$ into a nilpotent $J'$; $t_{C,J}$ is additive for the $J$-adic evaluations of $F$ and $F'$; and, for every $d\in D$, $t_{C,J}$ intertwines the evaluations of $\mathrm{act}\,d_1+_F(\mathrm{act}\,d_2\circ\varpi)$ for $X$ and for $X'$. Then there is a unique homomorphism $u\colon X\to X'$ (a pair of power series without constant term, a homomorphism $F\to F'$ of laws commuting with every $\mathrm{act}\,a$ and with $\varpi$) such that for all such $C$, $J$, $x$ and each coordinate $i$, $t_{C,J}(x)_i$ is the $J$-adic evaluation of $u_i$ at $x$.
--
--   This is the rigidity (functor-of-points) criterion for homomorphisms of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, in the shape needed in geometry: equivariance is assumed only for a $p$-adically dense set of elements $\alpha+\beta\Pi$ of $\mathcal O_D$, rather than for all of $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ and for $\Pi$ as in the variant `existsUnique_hom_apply_eq_adicEval_of_natural_of_isNilpotent` that it cites. It is used for fake elliptic curves, where a quaternionic homomorphism commutes on nilpotent thickenings only with the action of the elements of a fixed order, whose image in $\mathcal O_D$ is dense.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_existsUnique_hom_apply_eq_adicEval_of_natural_of_dense_of_isNilpotent.lean

